---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
---
<Base
  title="Contact · YOLO Electronics Repair"
  description="Reach YOLO Electronics Repair in West Sacramento by the request form, email or Instagram. Drop-off by appointment, mail-in welcome."
>
  <div>
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="sub">FORM OR EMAIL · SAME BENCH</p>
  </div>
  <p class="tag">Say what it is and what it's doing.</p>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Reach the bench</h2>
    <p class="note"><a href="/request/">Request a repair</a> with the form. It asks for what the bench needs and nothing else.</p>
    <div class="contact">
      <b>J1</b><span><a href="mailto:hello@yolorepair.com">hello@yolorepair.com</a></span>
      <b>J2</b><span><a href="https://instagram.com/yolo.repair">@yolo.repair</a> on Instagram</span>
    </div>
    <p class="note">The form or an email gets a repair started. No phone line.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>Where</h2>
    <p class="note">West Sacramento, California. Local drop-off covers West Sac and the rest of the 916, by appointment. Everyone else mails it in.</p>
    <p class="note">There's no street address here on purpose. You get it by email once there's a repair to bring or ship.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>If you'd rather email</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>What it is. Make and model if you have them.</li>
      <li>What it's doing, or not doing.</li>
      <li>What happened right before it quit.</li>
      <li>Drop-off or mail-in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note"><a href="/how-it-works/">How a repair goes from there</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
